1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,790
Invest in stocks with this thought,
and you'll never escape a crash.

2
00:00:05,170 --> 00:00:09,530
It's believing you're good at stocks
because you made money in a bull market.

3
00:00:09,910 --> 00:00:12,910
You made money, so you did
well. Why is that a problem?

4
00:00:13,290 --> 00:00:15,929
In a bull market, most
stocks rise together,

5
00:00:15,929 --> 00:00:18,148
so it's hard to tell skill from luck.

6
00:00:18,528 --> 00:00:24,147
Of the companies in today's S&P
500, 14 rose more than 2x in 2020.

7
00:00:24,527 --> 00:00:28,157
9 of them saw their stock price
cut in half within 2 years.

8
00:00:28,537 --> 00:00:29,738
Mistake luck for skill,

9
00:00:29,738 --> 00:00:32,871
and you'll bet bigger on one
stock and even borrow to do it.

10
00:00:33,251 --> 00:00:37,589
Then, when a crash comes, your gains and
even your principal collapse all at once.

11
00:00:37,969 --> 00:00:40,267
Just as ripe rice bows its head,

12
00:00:40,647 --> 00:00:44,986
the more you profit, call it luck
and set part of your gains aside.

13
00:00:45,366 --> 00:00:49,379
Only those who go slowly and
humbly like this survive a crash.

14
00:00:49,759 --> 00:00:52,959
Curious about other tests? Subscribe
and find them on the channel.
